# 3. SIMULTANEOUS TWO-AGENT EXECUTION

Use two specialist agents working in parallel wherever the environment supports subagents or parallel agent execution.

This is a deliberate requirement. Do not assign all work to one agent and then describe it as a two-agent workflow.

If the environment does not support spawning independent agents, use the closest available parallel orchestration mechanism. Be transparent in the final report about what was actually executed.

Both agents should inspect the repository and agree on the architecture before substantial implementation begins. After that, they should work concurrently and integrate continuously.

