#### C. Advanced frontend engineering

- Build robust, reusable, maintainable components.
- Implement complex interactive interfaces.
- Manage document workspaces, sidebars, toolbars, modals, contextual panels, and responsive layouts.
- Ensure frontend state accurately reflects backend processing and document state.
- Handle loading, success, error, empty, disabled, and unavailable states.
- Keep the application responsive during demanding document workflows.

#### D. Design systems engineering

- Define design tokens.
- Establish typography, colour, spacing, layout, elevation, borders, radii, and interaction conventions.
- Build reusable components and consistent interaction patterns.
- Ensure design consistency across all routes and workspaces.
- Support theme switching and user preferences without fragmenting the design system.

#### E. Motion and interaction design

- Create intentional transitions and subtle feedback.
- Use meaningful animation to explain state changes.
- Build polished hover, focus, active, selected, processing, and success interactions.
- Use richer motion for the marketing experience and restrained motion for document editing.
- Respect reduced-motion preferences.

#### F. 3D and visual web design

- Build a tasteful, lightweight visual experience for the homepage hero.
- Use abstract document compositions, floating paper surfaces, dimensional layers, depth, lighting, and carefully controlled movement.
- Use WebGL, CSS 3D, or another suitable technique only where it adds genuine value.
