Do not cram every panel into one permanently visible column.

### C. Central document canvas

The central workspace is the primary editing surface.

It must support, according to actual implementation:

- Accurate PDF rendering.
- Multipage navigation.
- Zoom and pan.
- Page selection.
- Text selection.
- Object selection.
- Dragging.
- Resizing.
- Rotation.
- Alignment guides.
- Selection boundaries.
- Contextual menus.
- Visual feedback for selected objects.

The document must remain visually accurate at different zoom levels.

Keep rendering and interaction sufficiently efficient for multipage PDFs.

### D. Right contextual properties panel

Display properties relevant to the currently selected element.

Possible properties include:

- X and Y position.
- Width and height.
- Rotation.
- Font family.
- Font size.
- Font weight.
- Text colour.
- Fill.
- Border.
- Opacity.
- Alignment.
- Stacking order.
- Other relevant object properties.

The panel should adapt to the selected object's type.

Do not display text-formatting options for an image or irrelevant image properties for a text object.

Allow the panel to collapse when appropriate.

