# 15. EDITOR ENGINEERING AND DOCUMENT ARCHITECTURE

Keep document rendering, editing state, and PDF serialization logically separated.

A useful conceptual architecture includes:

- Original PDF document.
- Rendered representation.
- Editable object model.
- Editor-managed objects.
- Annotation layer.
- Selection and interaction state.
- Page state.
- Editing operations.
- Undo/redo history.
- Export and serialization pipeline.

Evaluate libraries based on genuine capabilities.

PDF.js can be useful for rendering and text-layer support, but rendering alone does not provide a complete PDF editor.

pdf-lib or similar libraries may support selected PDF modifications, but do not assume they can reliably perform every low-level editing operation.

Investigate suitable combinations of libraries and services.

Pay attention to:

- Embedded fonts.
- Complex text layouts.
- Content streams.
- Images and masks.
- Transparency.
- Vector graphics.
- Form XObjects.
- Page resources.
- Annotations.
- Forms.
- Scanned documents.
- Multipage PDFs.
- Large files.
- Serialization integrity.

Do not compromise document correctness for implementation convenience.

