# 23. PERFORMANCE AND RELIABILITY

The application must remain usable with larger documents within the declared technical limits.

Prioritize:

- Fast initial page load.
- Lazy loading.
- Code splitting.
- Deferred loading of heavy PDF libraries.
- Efficient thumbnail rendering.
- Controlled memory use.
- Background processing.
- Responsive editor interaction.
- Upload reliability.
- Processing timeouts.
- Safe cancellation where supported.
- Graceful worker failure.
- Reliable output validation.

A failed processing job must not crash the entire application.

Do not load every PDF library and editor dependency on the homepage if it is not needed there.

Avoid performance-heavy decorative visuals.

