# 30. DEFINITION OF DONE

The product is complete only when all relevant conditions below are satisfied.

## Product

- The application runs.
- The homepage is complete.
- Tool discovery works.
- Guest access works.
- Optional accounts do not gate features.
- No monetization exists.
- No AI features exist.

## UI/UX

- The complete design system is implemented.
- The visual direction is consistent.
- The homepage has been refined.
- Tool workspaces are coherent.
- The editor has its full planned interface.
- Responsive layouts have been inspected.
- Accessibility has been considered and tested where possible.

## PDF functionality

- Implemented tools perform real operations.
- Files are validated.
- Processing is real.
- Outputs are valid.
- Downloads work.
- Editor operations are reflected in exported files where claimed.
- Unsupported operations are communicated accurately.

## Security and reliability

- Upload handling is validated.
- Temporary processing is isolated.
- Access controls are tested where applicable.
- Relevant application security controls are implemented.
- Processing failures are handled safely.
- Resource limits are applied consistently.

## QA

- The production build succeeds.
- The application starts.
- Core user journeys are tested.
- Real PDF workflows are tested.
- Generated documents are inspected.
- Visual defects are fixed.
- Regression checks are performed after significant fixes.

## Delivery

Provide:

1. A working preview URL if the environment supports one.
2. Local setup and run instructions.
3. A concise implementation summary.
4. A list of genuinely functioning tools.
5. PDF editor capabilities that have actually been implemented.
6. Tests performed and their results.
7. Any remaining technical limitations.
8. Any genuine blockers.

Do not claim browser-based visual verification if browser or computer-use tools were unavailable.

Do not claim an operation works unless it was implemented and tested.

